"comparison": "Both Goldman Sachs and Citi describe the establishment of specific frameworks and processes for operational risk control monitoring and testing to ensure compliance and mitigate risk. Goldman Sachs details 'control monitoring and testing' performed by dedicated teams in the first and second lines of defense to measure effectiveness and remediate issues. Similarly, Citi describes a 'Manager's Control Assessment (MCA) process' established within its Operational Risk Management Framework for the 'self-identification of significant operational risks' and 'assessment of the performance of key controls'. Both disclosures highlight a structured, framework-based approach to assessing control effectiveness, though Citi explicitly names the MCA process for self-identification while Goldman Sachs refers more generally to 'self-identified issues by our employees' being assessed alongside team findings.",
